  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Lockheed Martin obligated $10.5B in FY2026 to date across 140 awards, with an average award size of $75M and obligations up 0.8% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations climbed from $4.7B in FY21 to $10.5B in FY26, with interim dips in FY24 and rebounds in FY25 and FY26. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the dominant market, accounting for $9.6B of FY2026 to date obligations. Other notable NAICS categories include Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $733M, All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $62.7M, and several engineering and R&D categories in the $24.2M to $42.3M range. The current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations rather than total contract values. These figures show where federal dollars are concentrated and the relative scale of Lockheed Martin’s ongoing obligations across aerospace, missile, and technical services markets.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Why did Lockheed Martin’s obligations change year over year?",
        "body": "Lockheed Martin obligations were up 0.8% year over year in FY2026 to date. Fiscal-year obligations rose from $7.3B in FY24 to $10.4B in FY25 and then to $10.5B in FY26, reflecting larger award volumes or timing changes in the FY25 to FY26 window. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing accounted for the largest share of FY2026 to date obligations at $9.6B, which helps explain the overall increase."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where are Lockheed Martin’s federal contract dollars concentrated?",
        "body": "Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the largest market with $9.6B in FY2026 to date obligations. Other concentration points include Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $733M, All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $62.7M, Process, Physical Distribution, and Logistics Consulting Services at $42.3M, and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $42.1M."
      }
    ]
  },
